  'draft', 'foundation',
  'An 82-year-old woman with metastatic pancreatic cancer is on the ward. Over the last 48 hours she has become increasingly drowsy, is no longer eating or drinking, has developed Cheyne-Stokes breathing, and her hands and feet are cool and mottled. She is not in apparent distress. Her family ask whether anything more can be done.',
  'What is the most appropriate next step in her management?',
  array['dying phase','recognising dying','anticipatory care']
),
